Section B — Additional Restriction: 3-Year Non-Copy of
            Virtual GAS / Virtual Token Algorithm ("Addendum")
================================================================

This Addendum supplements Section A and applies ONLY to the
"Protected Algorithm" defined below. Where there is any conflict
between Section A and this Addendum, this Addendum prevails for
the Protected Algorithm during the Restriction Period.

1. Definitions

   1.1 "Protected Algorithm" means the virtual-liquidity bonding-curve
       mechanism implemented in this repository, including but not
       limited to:
       (a) the virtual GAS (virtualGAS / vGAS) and virtual Token
           (virtualToken / vToken) reserve model;
       (b) the derivation formulas in DuoLaunch._createSale:
             vToken = T * p² / BPS_DENOM / (2p - BPS_DENOM)
             vGAS   = R * (BPS_DENOM - p) / (2p - BPS_DENOM)
           where T = Constants.TOTAL_SUPPLY, R = targetRaise,
                 p = graduationBps;
       (c) the SaleInfo struct fields virtualGAS / virtualToken and
           any logic that computes effective reserves as
             GASReserve   = virtualGAS + GASRaised
             tokenReserve = virtualToken - tokensSold
           and derives prices / quotes from them;
       (d) the graduation parameterization (graduationBps / P,
           2p - BPS_DENOM constraint, maxTokens = T * p / BPS_DENOM)
           and any substantially similar re-implementation, translation
           to another language, or parameter-renamed copy.
       For avoidance of doubt, generic CP-AMM formula x*y=k in
       CurveMath.getAmountOut / getAmountIn is NOT protected by
       itself; only its combination with the virtual-reserve model
       above is protected.

   1.2 "Restriction Period" means three (3) calendar years starting
       from the Effective Date defined in §5.

   1.3 "Copy" means to reproduce, fork, port, or deploy the Protected
       Algorithm in any other project, protocol, contract, or product,
       whether verbatim or with immaterial modifications (renaming
       variables/functions, changing constants, translating comments,
       etc.) that retain the substance of the formulas/logic above.
       Independent creation without reference to this Software is not
       a "Copy" — the burden of proving independent creation lies with
       the copier.

2. Restriction

   During the Restriction Period, no person may Copy the Protected
   Algorithm without prior written authorization from the Licensor
   (as defined in §8). Prohibited acts include but are not limited to:
   deploying a separate on-chain contract that reuses the virtual
   GAS / virtual Token mechanism, or distributing off-chain code that
   implements it.

   Normal use of THIS Software (deploying, interacting with, or
   forking this repository as a whole to operate the Duo protocol
   itself) is NOT restricted. Contributing improvements back to this
   repository via pull request is encouraged and does not constitute
   a prohibited Copy.

3. Allowed Acts (not restricted)

   (a) Study, academic citation, and commentary with attribution;
   (b) Interfacing with / calling the deployed Duo contracts as a user
       or integrator (e.g., router / frontend integration);
   (c) Security review / audit of this Software.

4. Expiry / Conversion

   Upon expiry of the Restriction Period, the Protected Algorithm
   automatically becomes licensed under Section A (pure MIT) without
   further notice. No re-licensing action is required.

5. Effective Date and Expiry Date

   Effective Date: 2026-08-31
   Expiry Date:    2029-08-31 (00:00 UTC, 3 years after Effective Date)
   SPDX identifier for files containing the Protected Algorithm:
     SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
     Additional-Restriction: Duo-3Y-Algorithm-NC (see LICENSE Section B)

6. Enforcement

   A violation of this Addendum is both a breach of license (copyright
   infringement) and a breach of contract. The Licensor may seek
   injunctive relief, takedown (e.g., DMCA), and damages. Willful
   violation may be publicly disclosed.

7. Severability

   If any provision of this Addendum is held unenforceable, the
   remaining provisions remain in full effect and Section A continues
   to apply to all non-protected parts of the Software.

8. Pseudonymous Licensor / Anonymity Protection

   8.1 The "Licensor" / "Copyright Holder" is the pseudonymous
       collective operating as "Duo Finance" that controls this
       repository (github.com/DuoFinance/xDuo) and/or the canonical
       deployments of the Software. This is an anonymous/pseudonymous
       work within the meaning of the Berne Convention Art. 7(3) and
       17 U.S.C. §302(c) (and equivalent laws in other jurisdictions).
       Copyright subsists and is fully enforceable without disclosure
       of any natural person's legal name.

   8.2 No provision of this License requires the Licensor to reveal
       the identity of any natural person. Attribution or notices to
       the Licensor may be given via (in order of preference):
       (a) a GitHub issue/PR in this repository,
       (b) the contact published in this repository or its deployments,
       (c) a transaction / message signed by the canonical deployer
           or factory-owner address of the Duo protocol.
       A response signed by the same key or posted from the same
       GitHub organization is deemed a communication from the Licensor.

   8.3 Rights under this License (including the right to grant
       exceptions under §2 and to enforce under §6) may be exercised
       by the Licensor directly, or by any assignee or designated
       agent acting on the Licensor's behalf, without requiring the
       Licensor to de-anonymize. On-chain control of the repository
       or of the canonical DuoLaunch / factory deployer is prima facie
       evidence of authority; the Licensee shall not challenge standing
       solely on grounds of pseudonymity.

   8.4 Pseudonymity does not limit liability protections: Section A
       §2 disclaimer applies equally to the pseudonymous Licensor,
       its contributors, and its agents. No personal liability attaches
       to any undisclosed natural person by virtue of being part of
       the collective; liability, if any, is limited to the Licensor
       as defined above.

   8.5 Term and anonymity are independent: protection under this
       License lasts for the full copyright term (not shortened by
       anonymity), and the 3-year Restriction Period in §5 runs
       regardless of whether the Licensor later chooses to reveal
       identities.
